From 60ea25abefc833b7319b0e667a991a3fed3128b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aws-abigailfernandes <abigailferns94@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Apr 2026 12:41:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/24] feat: Make dynamo tests device-agnostic for PrivateUse1
 backends (#31)

* feat: Make dynamo tests device-agnostic for PrivateUse1 backends

Replace CUDA-specific code in 24 dynamo test files with device-agnostic
equivalents, enabling PrivateUse1 backends to run these tests without
monkey-patching.

- Replace device=cuda with device_type, .cuda() with .to(device_type)
- Replace torch.cuda.Stream/Event with torch.get_device_module(device_type)
- Replace torch.cuda.synchronize/current_stream with torch.accelerator APIs
- Replace @requires_cuda with @requires_accelerator where appropriate
- Add @requires_cuda to tests that use CUDA-specific APIs in test body
- Add device_type module-level constant using torch.accelerator
- Add COMPILE_BACKEND/get_compile_backend() to common_utils.py
- Add requires_accelerator_and_triton to triton_utils.py
